{%- comment -%}
  snippets/portal-nav.liquid — the account navigation (spec task 19.1, design §17.4).

  Requirements 4.12, 17.3, 17.4, 17.8, 17.10, 25.6, 25.9.

  ── ONE `<nav>`, THREE PRESENTATIONS ──────────────────────────────────────────
  §17.4 designs desktop, tablet and mobile separately because the constraints
  differ. They are NOT three markup trees: that would triple the DOM, put the same
  link on the page three times for a screen reader, and let the three drift.

  One list is rendered. CSS turns it into a vertical rail at ≥990 px, a horizontal
  scrolling row at 750–989 px, and a fixed bottom bar below 750 px. The bottom bar
  shows the first four entries plus **More**; the four demoted entries are hidden
  from the bar and reachable through the sheet, which renders the SAME hrefs.

  ── WHY THE BAR IS LIQUID AND NOT JAVASCRIPT ──────────────────────────────────
  Task 19.1: "rendered by Liquid so it survives any script failure". The bottom bar
  is the only way to leave a section on a phone, so if it depended on the portal
  bundle then a JavaScript error would trap the customer on one page. It is markup
  and CSS only; the sole scripted part is the More sheet, and `<dialog>` degrades to
  a visible list when the script never runs (see `portal-more-sheet`).

  ── `aria-current` IS SERVER-RENDERED ─────────────────────────────────────────
  Requirement 17.10 and §17.4. The current entry is known at render time, so
  computing it in JavaScript would mean the first paint has no current entry and a
  screen reader reaching the nav before the bundle executes hears eight
  indistinguishable links.

  ── THE ACTIVE STATE IS NEVER COLOUR ALONE (Requirement 17.8) ─────────────────
  Three non-colour carriers, one per breakpoint: a leading-edge hairline on the
  rail, an underline on the tablet row, and heavier label weight on the bar. Colour
  accompanies each; none depends on it.

  ── TARGETS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Every link is ≥44×44 px with ≥8 px separation (Requirement 17.3), enforced in
  `athoor-portal.css` by min-height and gap rather than by padding guesswork.

  PARAMETERS
    current  the `nav_key` of the page being rendered
{%- endcomment -%}

<nav class="athoor-portal__nav" aria-label="Your account">
  <ul class="athoor-portal__nav-list" role="list">
    {%- comment -%}
      Order is §17.4's, and the first four are the bottom bar's four. Activity is
      deliberately absent: §17.4 nests it under Rewards, so it is reached from the
      Rewards section rather than being a ninth destination.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- assign nav_items = 'overview,orders,wishlist,rewards,referrals,fragrance,profile,settings' | split: ',' -%}
    {%- for item in nav_items -%}
      {%- liquid
        case item
          when 'overview'
            assign label = 'Overview'
            assign href = '/pages/my-athoor'
          when 'orders'
            assign label = 'Orders'
            assign href = '/pages/my-athoor-orders'
          when 'wishlist'
            assign label = 'Wishlist'
            assign href = '/pages/my-athoor-wishlist'
          when 'rewards'
            assign label = 'Rewards'
            assign href = '/pages/my-athoor-rewards'
          when 'referrals'
            assign label = 'Referrals'
            assign href = '/pages/my-athoor-referrals'
          when 'fragrance'
            assign label = 'Fragrance profile'
            assign href = '/pages/my-athoor-fragrance'
          when 'profile'
            assign label = 'Profile'
            assign href = '/pages/my-athoor-profile'
          when 'settings'
            assign label = 'Settings'
            assign href = '/pages/my-athoor-settings'
        endcase

        assign is_current = false
        if item == current
          assign is_current = true
        endif

        assign in_bar = false
        if forloop.index <= 4
          assign in_bar = true
        endif
      -%}
      <li class="athoor-portal__nav-item{% unless in_bar %} athoor-portal__nav-item--overflow{% endunless %}">
        <a
          class="athoor-portal__nav-link"
          href="{{ href }}"
          {% if is_current %}aria-current="page"{% endif %}
        >
          <span class="athoor-portal__nav-label">{{ label }}</span>
        </a>
      </li>
    {%- endfor -%}

    {%- comment -%}
      The fifth bottom-bar target. Hidden above 750 px, where all eight entries fit.
      A `<button>` because it opens a dialog rather than navigating — announcing it
      as a link would promise a page that does not exist.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <li class="athoor-portal__nav-item athoor-portal__nav-item--more">
      <button
        class="athoor-portal__nav-link athoor-portal__nav-link--more"
        type="button"
        data-portal-more-open
        aria-haspopup="dialog"
        aria-controls="AthoorPortalMore"
      >
        <span class="athoor-portal__nav-label">More</span>
      </button>
    </li>
  </ul>
</nav>
